--- INSTRUCTOR NOTES ---
ATTACK TYPE: Smishing (SMS Phishing) — Lecture Slide 16

PSYCHOLOGICAL TRIGGERS USED:
  1. Trust       — Impersonates legitimate postal service "EgyptPost"
  2. Urgency     — "within 24 hours" deadline
  3. Scarcity    — Package will be "returned" (loss aversion)
  4. Familiarity — Most people regularly receive packages

RED FLAGS:
  - Domain "delivery-eg-update.com" is NOT egyptpost.gov.eg
  - Real postal services use official domains and tracking portals
  - The URL collects personal information (address + likely payment for "fee")
  - Exploits the fact that many people are always expecting deliveries
  - Generic — no recipient name or specific package description

CORRECT RESPONSE:
  - Do NOT click the link
  - Go directly to the official EgyptPost website to check tracking
  - If expecting a package, call the courier's official customer service
  - Report the SMS as spam/phishing

